  "prefLabel": "Lab 202.03 De novo hearing",
  "priorExpiration": "2007-01-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lab 202.03 “De novo hearing” means a new hearing which is not bound by the findings and rulings of a previous hearing before the commissioner or hearing officer and which allows the parties to introduce new evidence or evidence not considered by the hearing officer or commissioner at the previous hearing, subject to the provisions of Lab 205.09.\n\nSource. #2264, eff 1-6-83; ss by #2935, eff 12-27-84, EXPIRED 12-27-90\n\nNew. #5235, eff 9-27-91, EXPIRED: 9-27-97\n\nNew. #6631, INTERIM, eff 11-16-97, EXPIRED: 3-16-98\n\nNew. #6806, eff 7-18-98; ss by #8682, INTERIM, eff 7-15-06, EXPIRED: 1-11-07\n\nNew. #8922-A, eff 7-1-07; ss by #14534, eff 3-12-26 (formerly Lab 202.02)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lab200.html"
